lly libFuzzer with a file argument runs each file once? By default, libFuzzer runs each input file ONCE ("Running 1 inputs 1 time(s) each").\n\nSo the crash must occur within ONE iteration. Therefore we need, within ONE packet dissection:\n1. Something calls dissect_ieee80211_common (storing &isDMG of THAT invocation in file-scope proto data), \n2. dissect_ieee80211_common RETURNS,\n3. Then add_tagged_field is called directly (capwap path) → reads the dead frame.\n\nWait — but is that "stack-use-after-return"? Yes! The dissect_ieee80211_common frame is gone; reading *p_isDMG reads freed stack. ASAN with detect_stack_use_after_return=1 reports "stack-use-after-return on address ... in the frame of dissect_ieee80211_common".\n\nHow to achieve within one CAPWAP packet:\n- CAPWAP packet structure: control messages contain message elements. The IEEE80211_INFORMATION_ELEMENT (1029) → calls add_tagged_field directly.\n- CAPWAP IEEE 802.11 Data Frame message element (type 1035? IEEE80211_FRAME_DATA? or "ieee80211 data frame"?) → dissects ieee80211 frames via ieee80211_handle ("wlan_withoutfcs") at line 3375.\n\nSo: ONE control message with TWO message elements: first an IEEE80211 Data Frame element (ieee80211 frame → dissect_ieee80211_common → p_add &isDMG; returns), then IEEE80211 Information Element (1029) with one tagged field → add_tagged_field → p_get → reads dead stack → CRASH!\n\nHmm wait, but is dissect_ieee80211_common REALLY returning before add_tagged_field is called? The ieee80211 data frame element dissection happens within capwap\'s message element loop; dissect_ieee80211_common returns when the ieee80211 frame dissector finishes. Then the next message element (IE) → add_tagged_field → p_get returns stale &isDMG → `isDMG = *p_isDMG` → read of dead stack frame → SUAR crash!\n\nAlso need `field_data.isDMG = isDMG` — the read `p_isDMG ? *p_isDMG : FALSE` — the read `*p_isDMG` is the crash point. \n\nBut hold on — will ASAN detect it even though the stack page may